- The note lists symptoms but omits a crucial duration, deterioration, severity, number of episodes, resolved-versus-current status, baseline-versus-new distinction, or relevant negative.
- The note mentions “red flags” generally but omits an actual specific positive red flag, disease-specific negative, or escalation trigger established in the transcript.
- The note records a plan but drops the reason that makes the plan safe, urgent, or clinically interpretable.
- The note includes historical details from which a clinician might infer a conclusion, but omits the actual assessment or working diagnosis stated in the consultation.

